Diagram E.1 — Conjecture A: structural mechanism

```
   LOGARITHMIC DISCOUNT ATTENUATES BOUNDARY PENALTY

   rank:   1       2       3       ...     k-1      k
   weight: 1     0.63    0.50     ...    w_{k-1}  w_k
                                            |       |
                                            v       v
                                       large w    small w_k
                                                  (log2(k+1) denominator)

   PREDICTOR f_hat:
       correctly places top (k-1)
       misplaces x_(k) -> x_sub (much worse)

   NDCG deficit:
       DeltaDCG = [rho(x_(k)) - rho(x_sub)] / log2(k+1)
                                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~
                                           DAMPENS penalty

   REGRET:
       R_k = [f(x_(k)) - f(x_sub)] / k
                                    ~~~~
                                    NOT dampened by log

   AS k GROWS (or pool structure arranged):
       NDCG -> 1 (deficit vanishes in denominator)
       R_k stays bounded away from 0 (fixed numerator ratio)
       => NDCG >= t and R_k/range >= eps simultaneously
