Diagram E.2 — Invalid vs. valid scaling arguments

```
   INVALID: scale f by large M
   ============================
       f -> M*f
       NDCG -> NDCG          (scale-invariant: numerator and Z_k
                              both scale by M)
       R_k/range -> unchanged (also scale-invariant)
       => cannot inflate R_k while preserving NDCG.
       This argument does NOT prove Conjecture A.

   VALID: vary pool structure with fixed delta/range
   ==================================================
       Top-k cluster: {M, M-delta, ..., M-delta}
       Tail: many low designs
       Let k grow while delta/range = fixed constant c.
       Then:
         NDCG deficit per boundary swap = c*range / log2(k+1)  -> 0
         Normalized regret per boundary swap = c/2            = const > 0
       => NDCG -> 1, R_k/range >= c/2.

   The proof must explicitly compute the NDCG limit
   and verify it exceeds t for the chosen parameters.
```

